    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "This is the Daily Seabull Podcast for Friday, March 3rd. I'm Virginia Allen, and that was South Carolina Congressman Ralph Norman. America is trillions of dollars in debt. Congress has until June to reach an agreement on spending and raise the debt ceiling. President Joe Biden says that he plans to raise taxes on the wealthy. But what would that mean for the economy? Congressman Norman joins me on the show today from the conservative political action conference in Washington, D.C. to discuss how Biden's policies have affected the economy and what Republicans' plan is to cut spending. Stay tuned for our conversation after this. Conservative women, conservative feminists. It's true, we do exist. I'm Virginia Allen, and every Thursday morning on problematic women, Lauren Evans and I sort through the news to bring you stories that are of particular interest to give conservative leaning or problematic women. That is women whose views and opinions are often excluded or mopped by those on the so-called feminist left. We talk about everything from pop culture to politics and policy. Search for problematic women wherever you get your podcasts. And we are also problematic on social media. So be sure to follow us on Instagram. It is my pleasure today to be joined by South Carolina, Congressman Ralph Norman. Congressman, welcome back to the",
