    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83178.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "Here's what's been frustrating to Virginia. We have not had any bipartisanship under Pelosi. I don't know whether we will have any agreement on anything. We're just two worlds apart. Take the border. Look at what that's doing to our economy. It's easy. It's not a difficult cure for it. You build a wall and have a designated point of entry. You don't let everybody in from every country on the planet. You don't do that. He's been unwilling to do that. He's been unwilling to cut anything. Look at the State of the Union where he basically didn't say anything. When he started mentioning, you know, the, he was, he should have, most presidents put their vision out for the country. Instead, he did and had more divisive rhetoric. He got into high luggage at the airports was expensive. How the cashier at a restaurant had non-compete clauses. I mean, it doesn't make any sense. So it's just a matter of us. We don't need the Democrats now. We need 218 to pass anything. We got a 222 seat majority, which is slim. But that's in a good way. I think we'll encourage us to have a budget that we can back up. We didn't make the changes that the Speaker has agreed to. It took a lot of fight and it took a lot of willpower by 20 Americans who I'm proud to serve with to get make that happen. And I think it'll be the results hopefully you will see and hopefully we'll be able to get the 218 to pass it.",
