    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83178.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "My priority is making sure that South Carolina is a recipient of people that are coming from other states that aren't like us. Florida is a recipient. They've got what the census has done has been great. What South Carolina has done is great. We have to make sure that we remain a state has less taxes, less government, and make it a business-friendly state. We have to make sure that South Carolina doesn't give its natural resources away. These public-private partnerships, a lot of time it's the public that gets hosed and the private sector is the one that makes off. We've got to treat South Carolina as the treasure that it is. We're 5.3 million people. We're going to increase because people want to come to what we have to offer, which is good government. for the most part, is a state that is rich and being business friendly to those coming in. But we've got to guard that. And we've got those in office across the nation that has let California go like they've gone. They let Gavin Newsom basically bankrupt that state. But that happens because of who you put in office. We've got to keep South Carolina concerned.",
